WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.800
I definitely would not want
to fall from this height.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.240
We need to get to the
hive out of the branches

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.560
and lower it down.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.760
We're going to bring it down.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.600
We're going to lower it.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.000
This thing is
heavy, yeah, I have it.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.920
Bees release pheromones when
they're threatened so Joseph

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.280
uses smoke to disrupt their
sense of smell and stop them

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.400
from swarming.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.400
The bees are acting up, but
the smoke is doing its job.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.520
HAZEN: Ok, we have
everything locked off up here.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.960
The hive is
almost to the ground.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.440
Suspended.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.040
We've got the hive
down but we're not

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.560
going in for the honey just yet.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.480
The Okiek know that the bees
are reluctant to fly at night,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.480
and are far more docile.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.520
So, for now we must wait
for the light to fade.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.360
Now is the time.
It's plenty dark enough now.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.320
It's not getting
any darker than this.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.880
So, by firelight, we're going
to dig right into that hive.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.520
They're really
buzzing around in there.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.480
The kind of bees these
are East African honeybees.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.640
A big hive like this
can have 40,000 bees.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.640
Being stung in
numbers can be fatal.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.960
If they swarm the
risk is very real.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.800
There's a trap door on
the bottom of this hive.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.760
They're blowing more
and more smoke in there.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.880
Heart of the hive
with the honey.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.360
There it is,
that's it right there.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.440
That's what
we're talking about.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.800
Those bees are angry now.
They're starting to fly out.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.360
Ba-ba-ba-ba! Aye!

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.040
HAZEN: Ahhh right in the
armpit, that's a bad one.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.320
The smoke is preventing a
swarm but some bees are

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.800
still going in for the attack.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.400
When they crawl on you.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.400
They just sting
whatever feels like skin.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.840
Ah! I've got one under my shirt,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.160
and I've already
been stung about,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.760
I don't know, six or seven
times, I don't know.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.560
These guys are
getting stung, too.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.160
They're working fast,
trying to get the honeycomb.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.920
Oh.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.440
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.800
Heavy with honey.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.960
And then those white parts,
those are little baby honeybees,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.800
which isn't honey,
but it is protein.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.000
Might seem like a lot of work
to get honey but think about it,

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.480
there is nothing out
here sweeter than honey.

